  "result": "Shell completion now handles `#` correctly. The cause was `split_arg_string` in `src/click/shell_completion.py`: it uses `shlex`, which treats `#` as the start of a comment by default and drops the rest of the line. I set `lex.commenters = \"\"` there.\n\nI added two cases to `test_split_arg_string` in `tests/test_parser.py` (`a#b` and a leading `#a`). `tests/test_parser.py` and `tests/test_shell_completion.py` pass (67 tests); I didn't run the full suite.\n\nI also added an \"unreleased 8.5.1\" entry to `CHANGES.md`, since 8.5.0 was already released. I didn't touch `docs/`, because this is a bug fix with no new behavior to document.",
